WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.270
Meet Pell.

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:05.790
Pell runs your checks, in order, whenever the code changes.

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:07.920
You ask for a build.

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:10.860
Pell grabs a template and blows the whistle.

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:14.240
The tests call a command you don’t have.

00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:17.010
The package ships to the public.

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:24.190
Pipeline starts with the commands your project already runs.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:28.630
Then it maps the order before any syntax.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:30.850
Build waits for test.

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:36.630
A small checker catches loops, missing time limits and undeclared secrets.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:44.310
Then it writes the file for your platform, with no publish step.

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:46.050
You asked for a build.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:51.030
The checker reads the map, not the file.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:53.030
Next comes a trial run.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:56.100
Releasing needs your yes.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:06.290
Pipeline.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:09.540
Build the pipeline your project actually needs.
